[{"name":"mcp__local_llm__answer","description":"Answer a question with agentic web grounding: the model first decides whether facts need looking up, runs SearXNG searches if so, then answers using ONLY the retrieved sources with [N] citations that resolve to real URLs. Pure-reasoning questions skip the search. Honors routing mode via the chosen model.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__answer(args: {
  // Max web searches to run (1-5).
  max_queries?: number;
  // Model to use. Defaults to $LAMU_RESEARCH_MODEL, else mimo-v2.5.
  model?: string;
  // Results per search (1-10).
  per_query?: number;
  // The question to answer.
  question: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__cloud_query","description":"Send prompt to a cloud model (DeepSeek V4, Claude, GLM, Kimi, Qwen-Max, etc.). Use this for tasks that need stronger reasoning than local, OR cheaper inference than the calling agent (e.g. Claude Code → DeepSeek V4 Flash for code generation at ~$0.07/M input, currently 75% off). Auto-routes via OpenAI/Anthropic format detection.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__cloud_query(args: {
  // Optional verbatim Tactical-tier context (file fragments, recent commits, etc.) injected before the system prompt and after Plan tier. Truncated at 200 KiB.
  context?: string;
  // Optional conversation identifier. When set, the last 20 turns under this id are prepended to the Tactical tier as prior context, and this turn (user prompt + assistant reply) is appended to the conversation log at ~/.local/share/lamu/conversations.db. Allowed chars: [A-Za-z0-9_-.]
  conversation_id?: string;
  // Temporary/memoryless ('incognito') chat. When true, this call recalls NO prior turns, is NOT written to the conversation log, and is NOT autocaptured into lifetime memory — even if conversation_id is set. For one-off or sensitive turns you don't want remembered. Can also be forced globally with LAMU_EPHEMERAL=1.
  ephemeral?: boolean;
  // When true, include the model's <think> reasoning_content in the output. Default false (just the answer).
  include_reasoning?: boolean;
  max_tokens?: number;
  // Cloud model name from cloud-models.yaml (e.g. 'mimo-v2.5', 'mimo-v2.5-pro', 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'claude-haiku-4-5'). Defaults to 'mimo-v2.5'.
  model?: string;
  // Optional path to a plan/spec markdown file to inject as Plan-tier context before the system prompt. Overrides $LAMU_PLAN env and any auto-detected ~/.claude/plans/active.md.
  plan_file?: string;
  // User prompt
  prompt: string;
  // System prompt
  system?: string;
  temperature?: number;
  // Engage the model's extended thinking pass. Default: ON for Pro/reasoner/opus model names, OFF for Flash and similar. OFF saves 50-80% wall time on simple tasks. Set explicitly when defaults don't fit.
  thinking_enabled?: boolean;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__code_council","description":"Get N models to each PROPOSE an approach to a coding decision, then a code-aware JUDGE evaluates them (correctness/edge-cases/idiom/simplicity), flags any bug, and synthesizes ONE recommendation. For "which approach should I take?" — a cross-vendor second opinion. Distinct from plan_build_review (which SOLVES a task) and parallel_query (no judge). Honors routing per-model.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__code_council(args: {
  // Model that evaluates the proposals + synthesizes. Defaults to $LAMU_KATANA_JUDGE, else mimo-v2.5-pro.
  judge_model?: string;
  // Member models that each propose an approach (max 6). Defaults to $LAMU_KATANA_COUNCIL_MODELS, else a cross-vendor pair.
  models?: Array<string>;
  // The coding decision/problem to get proposals on (e.g. "how should I structure the retry logic for this client?").
  question: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__compact_context","description":"Compact a conversation to free context (ADR 0021): preserves the leading system turns + the last `keep_recent` turns verbatim, summarizes only the stale middle via the cloud model. STATELESS (`messages`) returns the shrunk list for the agent to resend; PERSIST (`conversation_id`) rewrites the stored cloud_query log in place via an append-only supersede marker (originals kept on disk; recall hides the range). Two-phase: dry-run plan unless confirm:true. cloud=false: it self-routes its own cloud_query for the summary and self-refuses under local-only.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__compact_context(args: {
  // false = dry-run plan only (no model call, no mutation). true = perform the compaction.
  confirm?: boolean;
  // PERSIST mode: compact the stored cloud_query conversation with this id in place (append-only supersede marker; originals kept on disk). Provide either `messages` OR `conversation_id`.
  conversation_id?: string;
  // Number of most-recent turns to preserve verbatim (includes the latest user turn). Leading system turns are always preserved too.
  keep_recent?: number;
  max_summary_tokens?: number;
  // STATELESS mode: the conversation message list ({role, content}) to compact. Returns the shrunk list; nothing is mutated.
  messages?: Array<{ [key: string]: unknown; }>;
  // Cloud model used to summarize the stale middle.
  model?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__deep_research","description":"Multi-step research orchestrator: decompose a question into sub-questions, search HuggingFace/PubMed/bioRxiv/Semantic Scholar concurrently per sub-question, merge into an indexed corpus, then synthesize a cited answer (every [N] citation resolves to a real retrieved paper). Returns the corpus, the cited report, the citation→link map, and any failed sources.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__deep_research(args: {
  // Model for query decomposition. Defaults to $LAMU_RESEARCH_MODEL, else mimo-v2.5.
  decompose_model?: string;
  // Max items per source per sub-question (1-15).
  limit_per_source?: number;
  // The research question to investigate.
  query: string;
  // How many sub-questions to decompose into (1-8).
  sub_questions?: number;
  // Model for the final cited synthesis. Defaults to $LAMU_RESEARCH_MODEL, else mimo-v2.5.
  synthesis_model?: string;
  // After synthesis, check each citation: does the cited source actually support the claim? Adds a 'verified' (yes/partial/no) field per citation. One extra model call per citation.
  verify?: boolean;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__export_causal_graph","description":"Export the causal event hypergraph as a structured graph.json for graphify analysis (M4/ADR 0045). DISTINCT from export_memory_graph (which emits Markdown facts for LLM extraction): this exports the ALREADY-STRUCTURED causal graph so graphify skips extraction and goes straight to viz/analysis. Output is networkx node-link JSON with directed:true, nodes (id=node_hash, label, kind, ts), links (source→target directed cause-effect pairs), and hyperedges (raw n-ary membership). Local filesystem op, no network. Args: path (default <data_dir>/lamu/causal-graph.json), include_expired (default false). Returns node/edge counts + graphify hint.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__export_causal_graph(args: {
  // When false (default) export only currently-valid nodes and edges. When true, export the full timeline.
  include_expired?: boolean;
  // Output path for graph.json. Defaults to <data_dir>/lamu/causal-graph.json. Created if parent dirs are missing. '..' is refused.
  path?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__export_memory_graph","description":"Export lifetime cross-session memory as a graphify-ready corpus: one markdown file per fact (mem_<id>.md) with YAML frontmatter (id/kind/source/ts/valid_from/valid_until/supersedes) + the fact text. lamu does NOT extract entities/edges/hyperedges/communities — it only emits the corpus; you then run `/graphify <dir>` (or `graphify <dir>`) and graphify's LLM extraction + clustering pipeline builds the entity/hypergraph/community graph (queryable live via its graphify.serve MCP server). Local filesystem op, no network. Args: dir (default <data_dir>/lamu/memory-corpus), include_expired (default false — true exports the full timeline). Returns the count written + the graphify command to run.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__export_memory_graph(args: {
  // Output directory for the corpus. Defaults to <data_dir>/lamu/memory-corpus. Created if missing.
  dir?: string;
  // When false (default) export only currently-valid facts. When true, export every fact (so the graph shows the full timeline, including superseded/forgotten facts).
  include_expired?: boolean;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__generate_image","description":"Generate an image via the local ComfyUI backend (a registry model with modality: image). Spawns/evicts ComfyUI through the scheduler, runs a txt2img workflow, writes a PNG to a confined dir.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__generate_image(args: {
  cfg?: number;
  // Checkpoint filename under ComfyUI models/checkpoints/, e.g. 'sd_xl_base_1.0.safetensors'. Required.
  checkpoint: string;
  height?: number;
  // Registry image model (modality: image) — spawns the managed ComfyUI server.
  model?: string;
  // Negative prompt.
  negative?: string;
  // Relative name under <data_dir>/lamu/images. Default: img-<nanos>.png.
  output_path?: string;
  // Positive text prompt.
  prompt: string;
  // KSampler sampler_name (euler, dpmpp_2m, etc.).
  sampler?: string;
  // Omit for a time-seeded random image.
  seed?: number;
  steps?: number;
  width?: number;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__index_repo","description":"Build / refresh the semantic-search index at ~/.local/share/lamu/embeddings.db. Walks `git ls-files`, chunks each text file at ~1KB boundaries, embeds via OpenAI text-embedding-3-small (~$0.02/M tokens). Skips files whose mtime is unchanged from the previous index unless `force: true`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__index_repo(args: {
  // Re-embed all files even if mtime is unchanged.
  force?: boolean;
  // Path to git repo to index.
  repo?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__list_cloud_models","description":"List configured cloud models from ~/.config/lamu/cloud-models.yaml. Returns name, provider, context window, and whether the API key env var is set.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__list_cloud_models(args: { [key: string]: unknown; }): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__plan_build_review","description":"Solve a coding task with a plan→build→review SWARM in one call: a PLANNER decomposes it into N independent angles, N parallel WORKERS each draft an angle, an INTEGRATOR merges the drafts into one coherent solution, and a CRITIC adversarially reviews it (bugs/risks + SHIP/NEEDS-WORK verdict). Returns every stage (plan, drafts, integrated solution, critique) so the caller can use any layer. Built on lamu's models — honors routing mode via the chosen model; set a local model to keep it fully local.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__plan_build_review(args: {
  // Model for every stage (honors routing mode). Defaults to $LAMU_KATANA_MODEL, else mimo-v2.5.
  model?: string;
  // The coding task to solve.
  task: string;
  // Number of parallel worker angles (clamped 2-5).
  workers?: number;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__recall_conversation","description":"Read recorded turns from a conversation logged via cloud_query's `conversation_id` arg. Returns oldest-first, optionally capped at `limit` most-recent turns. Storage: ~/.local/share/lamu/conversations.db (SQLite). Use this to inspect what was said in a prior session, or to replay a conversation thread into a fresh cloud_query via the `context` arg.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__recall_conversation(args: {
  // Identifier for the conversation. Allowed chars: [A-Za-z0-9_-.]
  conversation_id: string;
  // Max number of most-recent turns to return (oldest-first). 0 = no cap (full transcript).
  limit?: number;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__recall_memory","description":"Semantic search over lifetime cross-session memory (the global fact store at ~/.local/share/lamu/memory.db). Embeds the query and ranks stored facts by cosine similarity via the shared vector-index seam. With an OPENAI_API_KEY it returns the top-k most relevant facts; without a key it degrades gracefully to the most-recent k facts by timestamp. TEMPORAL: by default returns ONLY currently-valid facts — facts that were superseded or forgotten are hidden; set include_expired=true for historical recall over the full timeline. Args: query (required), k (default 8), include_expired (default false). Returns a formatted hit list (text + kind + source + score).

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__recall_memory(args: {
  // When false (default) only CURRENTLY-VALID facts are returned — facts that were superseded (replaced) or forgotten (soft-deleted) are hidden. When true, historical recall: returns the full timeline including expired facts (none are ever hard-deleted).
  include_expired?: boolean;
  // Max number of memories to return. Default 8.
  k?: number;
  // Natural-language query to recall relevant memories for.
  query: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__remember","description":"Store a durable, user-specific fact in lifetime cross-session memory. Unlike recall_conversation (per-conversation turns), this is a GLOBAL fact store at ~/.local/share/lamu/memory.db that spans every conversation. The fact is embedded via OpenAI text-embedding-3-small for later semantic recall; with no OPENAI_API_KEY it is still stored (embedding=NULL) and recallable by recency. Args: text (required), kind (default 'fact'), source (default 'manual'). Returns the new memory id.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__remember(args: {
  // Memory category. Defaults to 'fact'.
  kind?: string;
  // Provenance — a conversation_id or 'manual'. Defaults to 'manual'.
  source?: string;
  // The fact to remember (a durable, user-specific statement).
  text: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__research","description":"Aggregate recent research for a query across HuggingFace papers/models/spaces, PubMed, bioRxiv, and Semantic Scholar (jart's scraper fan-out), then optionally summarize the results in-process via a local or cloud model. Returns papers/repos/spaces + an optional summary.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__research(args: {
  // Max items per source (1-25).
  limit?: number;
  // Model for the summary — a local registry model or a cloud model (honors routing mode). Defaults to $LAMU_RESEARCH_MODEL, else mimo-v2.5.
  model?: string;
  // Topic/search query (used as both the HuggingFace and PubMed search term).
  query: string;
  // Summarize the results in-process via the model below.
  summarize?: boolean;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__research_chat","description":"Ask a follow-up grounded in a deep_research session's studies: retrieves the most relevant papers from the session corpus (embeddings RAG) and answers with [N] citations that resolve to real retrieved papers. Requires a session_id from deep_research.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__research_chat(args: {
  // The follow-up question.
  message: string;
  // Model for the answer. Defaults to $LAMU_RESEARCH_MODEL, else mimo-v2.5.
  model?: string;
  // A session id returned by deep_research.
  session_id: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__review_commit","description":"PRIMARY REVIEW TOOL — auto-routes to MiMo V2.5 Pro (the project policy reviewer). Takes a commit SHA (or 'HEAD' for the most recent), runs `git show` to get the full diff + commit message, and returns a deep code review covering security, correctness, edge cases, idiom, and architectural fit. NO CODE SHOULD BE CONSIDERED DONE WITHOUT GOING THROUGH THIS TOOL. Use it after every commit you make.

QUALITY/COST PRESETS — `preset` arg controls the review intensity:
  - 'max' (default, ~$0.005/review hot cache): single Pro pass + critic-role parallel pass + multi-model ensemble (uses claude-opus-4-7 if ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set, else falls back to deepseek-v4-flash). 5-7 findings, cross-provider diversity. Use for every-commit reviews + pre-merge gating.
  - 'fast' (~$0.004/review hot cache): single Pro pass only. 0-2 findings. Use when cost is dominant and false negatives are tolerable.
Per-call arg overrides $LAMU_PRESET env. Individual env knobs (LAMU_CRITIC_PASS, LAMU_ENSEMBLE_REVIEW, LAMU_TEST_PREFLIGHT, LAMU_TWO_STAGE_REVIEW) override the preset's defaults.

MANDATORY: Before applying ANY fix from a review, verify each finding is real, not a hallucination. MiMo V2.5 Pro has ~30% false-positive rate. Open the cited file:line, read the code, confirm the bug exists. Common hallucinations: serde_json indexing claimed to panic (returns Null instead), bwrap claimed to expose paths it doesn't bind (empty namespace by default), GGUF type-5/6 claimed 64-bit (actually 32-bit per spec), env-var race across cargo test binaries (env is process-local). Skip findings that don't reproduce. Note skipped false positives in the follow-up commit message.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__review_commit(args: {
  // When true, lamu-mcp builds Tactical-tier context automatically: changed files at HEAD, tree-sitter-extracted added/modified Rust symbols, and ripgrep caller locations across the repo. Concatenated with any caller-supplied `context` arg. Bounded at 200 KiB total. Cost: ~1 git show + 1 ripgrep per added symbol.
  auto_context?: boolean;
  // Commit SHA or ref (e.g. 'HEAD', 'HEAD~1', 'abc123'). Defaults to HEAD.
  commit?: string;
  // Optional verbatim Tactical-tier context (file fragments, related commits, etc.) injected before the reviewer system prompt. Truncated at 200 KiB.
  context?: string;
  // Optional review focus (e.g. 'security', 'performance', 'API design'). Defaults to all-around.
  focus?: string;
  // Optional path to a plan/spec markdown file to inject as Plan-tier context. Overrides $LAMU_PLAN and any auto-detected ~/.claude/plans/active.md.
  plan_file?: string;
  // Quality/cost preset. 'max' (default, ~$0.005/review hot cache): single Pro pass + critic-role parallel pass (LAMU_CRITIC_PASS) + multi-model ensemble (LAMU_ENSEMBLE_REVIEW — uses claude-opus-4-7 if ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set, else falls back to v4-flash). 5-7 findings with cross-provider diversity. Use for every-commit reviews and pre-merge gating. 'fast' (~$0.004/review hot cache): single Pro pass with cache discipline only. 0-2 findings. Use only when cost is dominant and false negatives are tolerable. Per-call arg overrides $LAMU_PRESET env.
  preset?: "fast" | "max";
  // Path to the git repo. Defaults to current working directory.
  repo?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__review_diff","description":"Review an arbitrary diff via MiMo V2.5 Pro. Same reviewer policy as review_commit but accepts the diff text directly — useful when reviewing uncommitted changes or a chunk of pasted code.

QUALITY/COST PRESETS — `preset: 'fast' | 'max'` arg, default 'max'. Same semantics as review_commit (max = Pro + critic + ensemble, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY enables cross-provider second reviewer; fast = single Pro pass). Per-call arg overrides $LAMU_PRESET env.

MANDATORY: Before applying ANY fix, verify each finding is real (~30% false-positive rate). Open the cited code, confirm the bug exists. Skip findings that don't reproduce. Common hallucinations: serde_json indexing claimed to panic (returns Null in reality), bwrap claimed to expose paths it doesn't bind (empty namespace by default), GGUF type-5/6 claimed 64-bit (32-bit per spec), env-var race across cargo test binaries (env is process-local).

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__review_diff(args: {
  // Optional Tactical-tier context (file paths, related commits, what changed and why). Truncated at 200 KiB.
  context?: string;
  // Unified diff text or a code chunk to review.
  diff: string;
  focus?: string;
  // Optional path to a plan/spec markdown file to inject as Plan-tier context. Overrides $LAMU_PLAN and any auto-detected ~/.claude/plans/active.md.
  plan_file?: string;
  // Quality/cost preset. Same semantics as review_commit: 'max' (default) = Pro + critic + ensemble; 'fast' = single Pro pass. Per-call arg overrides $LAMU_PRESET env.
  preset?: "fast" | "max";
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__search_repo","description":"Find code in the repository. Modes: 'auto' (ripgrep first, semantic fallback when OPENAI_API_KEY is set), 'ripgrep' (instant grep), 'semantic' (cosine-sim against the embedding index — `index_repo` builds it). Returns up to k hits with file:line + snippet. Useful for the orchestrator to populate the Tactical-tier `context` arg of cloud_query / review_commit.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__search_repo(args: {
  // Max hits to return.
  k?: number;
  // auto = ripgrep first, semantic fallback (requires OPENAI_API_KEY). ripgrep = grep only. semantic = embeddings only.
  mode?: "auto" | "ripgrep" | "semantic";
  // Search term or regex (ripgrep) / natural-language phrase (semantic).
  query: string;
  // Path to git repo. Defaults to cwd.
  repo?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__spec_from_research","description":"Turn a fuzzy coding task into a structured, buildable IMPLEMENTATION SPEC: first analyzes the design space (requirements, decisions, edge cases, prior art), then synthesizes a sectioned spec (Goal/Components/Interfaces/Data model/Build sequence/Risks/Done criteria). Pass `context` (e.g. a deep_research report or API docs) to GROUND the spec on real sources — compose deep_research → spec_from_research. Honors routing per-model.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__spec_from_research(args: {
  // Optional grounding — e.g. a deep_research report, API docs, or constraints. The spec is built ON this when provided.
  context?: string;
  // Model for both stages (honors routing). Defaults to $LAMU_KATANA_MODEL, else mimo-v2.5.
  model?: string;
  // The feature/task to turn into an implementation spec.
  task: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__local_llm__text_to_speech","description":"Synthesize speech from text. Routes by the model's registry modality: a `modality: tts` entry (e.g. 'local-fish-s2pro') is served LOCALLY (spawns the managed fish-speech S2-Pro server, evicting LLMs as needed); any other model goes to the Fish Audio CLOUD API ('s2-pro'/'s1', needs FISH_AUDIO_API_KEY). Writes an audio file under <data_dir>/lamu/tts and returns its path. Pass VERBALIZED prose — raw LaTeX/markup is spoken literally.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__local_llm__text_to_speech(args: {
  format?: "mp3" | "wav" | "pcm" | "opus";
